Description: WLAN Pi menu service
 Headless menu service for the WLAN Pi. It owns the menu manifests,
 sessions and jobs, and serves every surface (TUI, WebUI, front panel,
 mobile) over one authenticated WebSocket protocol on Unix sockets under
 /run/wlanpi-menud. Every device operation is delegated to wlanpi-core.
 .
 The service binds no TCP port and touches no hardware, so it installs
 and runs alongside wlanpi-fpms without interfering with it.
